# TEAM TRANSFER ONLY. The solo edition does not use this file: GitHub does not let a pull request's
# author approve it, so required code-owner review would block a one-person repository.
# When the repository gains a second maintainer, copy this to .github/CODEOWNERS, replace each
# placeholder with a real login, and turn on code-owner review and one required approval in the ruleset.

*                               @DRIVER-LOGIN @EVIDENCE-LOGIN @REVIEWER-LOGIN

# Agent behaviour is code. Profiles, instructions and MCP configuration change how every agent acts.
/.github/agents/                @REVIEWER-LOGIN @EVIDENCE-LOGIN
/.github/copilot-instructions.md @REVIEWER-LOGIN @EVIDENCE-LOGIN
/.github/instructions/          @REVIEWER-LOGIN @EVIDENCE-LOGIN
/.vscode/mcp.json               @REVIEWER-LOGIN @EVIDENCE-LOGIN
/mcp/                           @REVIEWER-LOGIN @EVIDENCE-LOGIN

# Quality gates. Changes here can silently weaken acceptance.
/.github/workflows/             @REVIEWER-LOGIN
/ci/                            @REVIEWER-LOGIN
/tests/                         @REVIEWER-LOGIN
/perf-budget.json               @REVIEWER-LOGIN
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @REVIEWER-LOGIN
